outrage is growing in beirut after last  week's deadly explosion  violent new protests erupted over the  weekend as demonstrators call for the  president  and government to resign at least 158  people were killed in the explosion and  more than 6  thousand injured mts tayab reports from  the lebanese capital  protesters stormed the gilded offices of  major government ministries  pillars of power they say only function  to prop up the corrupt political elite  thousands of the desperate and the  traumatized gathered in the heart of  their shattered city shouting  revolution but almost immediately were  met  with tear gas this isn't just protests  this is a call for a revolution to rise  up against the ruling class  they say destroyed their lives some here  are calling for blood  while others only want their leaders  who've been in power for decades  gone they don't care about the people we  want them all  out nearly half of beirut was devastated  in the massive explosion  caused by over 2 700 tons of ammonium  nitrate  carelessly stored at the downtown port  world leaders are pledging nearly 300  million dollars in emergency  humanitarian aid  including the u.s but there are strings  attached  no money unless economic and political  reforms  are made the question now is will this  criminally corrupt government  who hold on to power with a vice-like  grip let go  for cbs this morning infyostab beirut
 

